Ladybird resolves calc(64px / (300px / 1s)) to 0.213333s, as the other
engines do. Each of them evaluates the calculation tree recursively when
it computes the value, rather than relying on simplification to reduce
it: Gecko in GenericCalcNode::resolve_internal(), Blink in
CSSMathExpressionOperation::ComputeValueInCanonicalUnit(), and WebKit in
the evaluate() overloads of CSSCalcTree+Evaluation.cpp. All three keep
the specified value unsimplified, as Ladybird does.
